---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AdSlot from '../../components/AdSlot.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  currentPath="guide"
  title="User Guide & FAQ - fntx Web"
  description="Learn how to subset large CJK fonts, merge BMP and SIP planes, convert to WOFF2, and unpack/pack TTC collections locally in your browser."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl space-y-6 px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">User Guide & FAQ</h1>

    <section class="space-y-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">1. How do I subset a large CJK font for the web?</h2>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        Drop your source font (e.g. a 15–30 MB <code>.ttf</code>) into the workbench, switch to <strong>Subset / Merge</strong>, paste the characters you need, select <code>WOFF2</code>, and click Build. You can preview the output immediately in the browser before downloading.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">2. How do I merge BMP and SIP supplementary fonts?</h2>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        Your primary font covers <code>00000 - 0FFFF</code> by default. Click <strong>Add Source</strong> to attach a supplementary font (e.g. Extension B in <code>20000 - 2FFFF</code>), and fntx will subset each plane and merge them into one unified font.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">3. Are my font files uploaded to any server?</h2>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        Never. Every operation runs strictly inside a local WebAssembly Web Worker in your browser memory.
      </p>
    </section>

    <AdSlot lang="en" slotId="guide-bottom-en" />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
